{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.IdentityIHLFBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRSKBurnside"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.sum_map_dimHLF_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.sum_map_dimHLF_sq","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L224-L239","doc":"**`Σ_{λ ⊢ n} dimHLF(λ)² = n!` for every `n`** — the list-model dimension certificate that\n`dim_validated_le12` establishes by `decide` at `n ≤ 12`, now available at every `n`.\n\nThis is `rskBurnsideHolds_le12` run backwards: that theorem transports the `decide`-verified list\nidentity *up* to the abstract `Nat.Partition` index; this one transports the Robinson–Schensted\ntheorem (`QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnsideHolds`) *down* to the list index, through the same two bridges —\n`rskBurnsideHolds_iff_dimHLF` for the hook-length identification and `sum_map_partitionsOf` for the\nenumeration.\n\nConsumers that were capped at `n ≤ 12` only because `dim_validated_le12` was a finite check can use\nthis instead; `dim_validated_le12` remains the cheaper route inside its range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.rskBurnsideHolds_le12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.rskBurnsideHolds_le12","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L206-L216","doc":"**RSK/Burnside for `n ≤ 12`, on the genuine SYT count.**  `Σ_{p ⊢ n} dimSYT(p)² = n!` —\nthe `decide`-verified list-model dimension certificate `dim_validated_le12`, transported to the\nabstract `Nat.Partition` index through the enumeration bridge, and onto `dimSYT` through the\nhook-length bridge `dimSYT_eq_dimHLF` (via `rskBurnsideHolds_iff_dimHLF`).  No RSK\ncorrespondence is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.sum_map_partitionsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.sum_map_partitionsOf","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L198-L202","doc":"**Sum transport.** A sum of any `g : List ℕ → M` over the enumerator `partitionsOf n`\nequals the abstract sum over `Nat.Partition n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.toFinset_partitionsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.toFinset_partitionsOf","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L185-L196","doc":"**The enumeration bridge.** The finset underlying `partitionsOf n` is exactly the image of\n`Nat.Partition n` under `toList`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.partitionsOf_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.partitionsOf_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L180-L181","doc":"`partitionsOf n` has no duplicates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.mem_partitionsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.mem_partitionsOf","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L167-L178","doc":"**Membership in the enumerator.** `partitionsOf n` lists exactly the weakly-decreasing\npositive lists summing to `n` — the computable model of `Nat.Partition n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.partsFuel_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.partsFuel_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L136-L163","doc":"`partsFuel` enumerates without duplicates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.mem_partsFuel_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.mem_partsFuel_complete","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L91-L132","doc":"**Completeness.** Every weakly-decreasing list of parts in `[1, cap]` summing to `t`, of\nlength at most the fuel, appears in `partsFuel f t cap`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.mem_partsFuel_sound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge.mem_partsFuel_sound","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/PartitionsOfBridge.lean#L40-L68","doc":"Every member of `partsFuel f t cap` is a weakly-decreasing list of parts in `[1, cap]`\nsumming to `t`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}